{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790363757,"nonce":"aDZhWyjDzjJr+1iveIcA2mD82so=","title":"A local function named like a stdlib static was bound to that static","message":"`function append(v:Int) buf.add(...)` then `append(1)`: MIR's call lowering has several by-name fallbacks (qualified-name search, class-less static lookup, unique static by name and arity) that ran for any callee symbol without a function id, locals included. `append` with one argument uniquely matched sys.io.File.append (file_append_default), so the call went there with the wrong arguments and crashed or did nothing (Issue11800 CRASH, Issue11851, Issue11040, Issue4466; any local named append/write/...). Fix: a callee that is a local value bound in the function never takes a by-name path; it is called through its value. Also Context.getType of a bare generic now gives fresh unknowns for its parameters (Issue2521). Conformance 678 -\u003e 682, 0 LOST; compiler integration tests pass.","files":null}]}